    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy is delighted to present this charming, double-fronted three-bedroom residence to the market. Superbly positioned in the heart of Skerries, this distinctive property combines traditional streetscape character with an enviable coastal lifestyle. Featuring a handsome painted facade with classic sash-style windows and an elegant fanlight entrance, the home arrives on the market offering a sound structure and an exceptionally versatile layout. While immediately habitable, the interior presents an exciting blank canvas for prospective purchasers looking to modernise, upgrade, and create a bespoke dream home tailored to contemporary tastes.\n\nPassing through the main entryway, the interior accommodation extends across a light-filled single-level floor plan. The heart of the home centers around a spacious, living room anchored by a feature fireplace. To the right of the living space sits a bedroom, while to the left lie two additional double bedrooms, one featuring its own traditional fireplace detail. A quiet inner hallway toward the rear leads to a well-appointed family bathroom and opens into a spacious, light-filled eat-in kitchen that forms the primary dining and culinary hub of the property.\n\nStepping through the rear access, the property opens onto a completely private, low-maintenance paved courtyard. Enclosed by a magnificent, original natural stone boundary wall, this sunlit outdoor sanctuary provides a tranquil and secure haven ideal for morning coffee, alfresco dining, or container gardening, away from the hustle and bustle of daily life.\n\nThe location of this home is simply second to none, placing all the magic of Skerries right on your doorstep. Residents enjoy an effortless stroll to Skerries' vibrant town centre, renowned for its boutique shops, cosy cafes, award-winning restaurants, and lively pubs. The iconic Skerries Harbour, North and South beaches, and picturesque coastal walks are all within a few minutes' walk, while sports enthusiasts benefit from nearby sailing, golf, rugby, GAA, and tennis facilities. Commuters are exceptionally well-serviced by the nearby Skerries Train Station providing direct access to Dublin City Centre, alongside swift connections to the M1 motorway, M50, and Dublin Airport. This property represents a rare and remarkable opportunity to acquire a character home of real substance in one of North County Dublin's most coveted coastal addresses."
      },
      {
